{"id":237307595304789,"type":"album","name":"Sextant","artist":"Herbie Hancock","year":1973,"weight":19,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/58639-sextant.jpg","aoty":90,"aoty_user":83,"yt":"6Mz5rR0y0fM","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/herbie-hancock/sextant/","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/58639-herbie-hancock-sextant.php"},"desc":"Herbie Hancock's Sextant, released on March 30, 1973, stands as an album that redefined the boundaries of jazz fusion. This groundbreaking work emerged during a transformative period in jazz history, when traditional acoustic instruments were being augmented by electronic innovations. As Hancock's eleventh studio album and the final recording with his Mwandishi-era sextet, it featured an exceptional lineup including saxophonist Bennie Maupin, whose bass clarinet work would later influence countless woodwind players; trumpeter Eddie Henderson, known for his pioneering use of electronic effects in jazz; and trombonist Julian Priester, whose textural approach helped shape the album's unique soundscape. When Herbie ."},"artist_ref":{"id":57041058518848,"name":"Herbie Hancock","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Herbie_Hancock.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":265524373450282,"type":"genre","name":"jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1461,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":89886331015150,"type":"genre","name":"Jazz Fusion","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":240,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":18560543527384,"type":"genre","name":"Avant-Garde Jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":235,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":7248838886199,"type":"genre","name":"Jazz-Funk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":227,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":159918588106246,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Electronic","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":226,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":43001458719353,"type":"genre","name":"Afrofutu